# Arduino Nano-like

A deliberately generic Nano-compatible module used by the example project.
The origin is its upper-left header pin when the USB connector faces north.
Confirm the exact pinout and dimensions of the physical module before assembly.

The example assigns physical numbers around the perimeter: pins 1–15 run down
the left header and pins 16–30 run back up the right header. Clone and adjust
the definition when a particular Nano-compatible board uses different markings.
